 "id": "2026-11-04-abu-dhabi-talks",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Russia and Ukraine will sit down again next week. Can talks stop another winter of war?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff says Washington will mediate talks between Russia and Ukraine in Abu Dhabi on November tenth and eleventh. He says they will cover security arrangements, easing the fighting, and humanitarian steps. Jared Kushner will co-lead the U.S. team."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "On Tuesday, the Kremlin confirmed it will take part. Spokesman Dmitry Peskov named Vladimir Medinsky as Russia's chief negotiator. Reports say it is the first U.S.-mediated round since February, when the Iran war stalled the process."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Doubts remain. On Monday, Ukraine accused Russia of using a six-day local ceasefire around Oleshky to reinforce its positions. Russia has not commented in the reports so far. Neither side has announced concessions."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Abu Dhabi talks lead to a ceasefire this year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
