 "upload": {
  "title": "Russia and Ukraine Talk Again in Abu Dhabi. Will It Work? #shorts",
  "description": "U.S. envoy Steve Witkoff announced on November 3 that the United States will mediate talks between Russia and Ukraine in Abu Dhabi on November 10 and 11. According to Witkoff, the agenda covers post-war security arrangements, de-escalation and humanitarian steps; Witkoff and Jared Kushner lead the U.S. delegation. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov confirmed on November 3 that Russia will take part, with Vladimir Medinsky as chief negotiator. Reports describe it as the first U.S.-mediated round since February, when the war with Iran stalled the process. Ukraine accused Russia on November 2 of using a six-day local ceasefire in the occupied Oleshky area of Kherson region to reinforce its positions; Russia's response was not found in the reports. No concessions from either side have been announced. Details could still change before the talks begin.\n\nSources:\nAxios, Nov 3, 2026: U.S., Russia and Ukraine to resume peace talks in Abu Dhabi next week, Witkoff says\nCNBC, Nov 3, 2026: Russia confirms new Ukraine peace talks as Melania Trump prepares to host ceasefire meeting\nThe Hill, Nov 3, 2026: Witkoff announces Abu Dhabi peace negotiations\nU.S. News / Reuters, Nov 3, 2026: Kremlin confirms trilateral Ukraine peace talks in Abu Dhabi next week\nThe Moscow Times, Nov 3, 2026: U.S.-mediated Ukraine peace talks to resume in Abu Dhabi next week\n\n#geopolitics #Ukraine #Russia #AbuDhabi",
